{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA → 48.5% acc), the most fundamental uncertainty is whether the image modality carries independent predictive signal. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest single-variable comparison to the RNA-only baseline, isolating the effect of modality. If image-only performs comparably or better, it strongly motivates investing in multimodal configurations; if it performs poorly, it tells us the image channel is weak and we should prioritize improving the RNA side (better encoders, multiprofile). This decomposition is essential before testing multimodal fusion, because without knowing each modality's standalone contribution, we cannot interpret whether a multimodal result reflects genuine synergy or simply dominance of one channel. Under the limited budget, resolving this foundational question maximizes the information gained per experiment and guides all subsequent choices."
}

